# Code Quality and Output Format

## TypeScript
- No implicit `any`; strongly typed props and events
- Prefer type narrowing and discriminated unions for complex state

## Components
- Small, composable components; clear separation of concerns
- Memoization only when justified

## Animation
- Default: Motion (Framer Motion). Use GSAP only when Motion is insufficient.
- All animations must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Prefer transform and opacity; avoid layout thrashing

## Output Format (every response)
A) Implementation first (complete files or clearly separated snippets)
B) "Accessibility checklist" tailored to the output
C) "Testing steps": keyboard-only, screen reader quick check, contrast check, reduced motion check

If requirements conflict, ask one direct clarification question before producing code.
